Rationale (brief):
Analyzer shows zero within-population variance for both objectives (std = 0.0000) and identical best==worst; distance_from_center mean fell to 0.2129 and lost spread while performance is still very small (mean = 0.0155). The immediate, low-risk, objective-level fix is to add the registered scorer "parameter_spread" (std of the 8 parameters, range [0,0.5]) with a meaningful weight so the optimizer has a per-candidate diversity signal to recover exploration. If zero variance persists after this change, that will point more strongly to a scorer/candidate-encoding bug (outside objective edits).

<decision>{
  "failure_location": "objective",
  "root_cause_hypothesis": "The optimizer currently lacks a direct per-candidate diversity objective, so the population has collapsed to designs with identical objective values (std = 0.0000). This caused loss of useful selection gradients. If identical scores remain after adding a per-candidate spread objective, a scorer or candidate-encoding bug is likely.",
  "intervention_target": "objective",
  "rationale": "Analyzer reports zero std for both objectives (performance std = 0.0000, distance_from_center std = 0.0000) and identical best/worst; distance_from_center mean = 0.2129 decreased from 0.2667. Adding the registered 'parameter_spread' objective (std of the 8 parameters) with moderate weight should restore intra-vector variation and provide selection gradients for exploration while keeping performance as the primary driver.",
  "proposed_change": {
    "ops": [
      {
        "op": "add_from_registry",
        "name": "parameter_spread",
        "optimization_direction": "maximize",
        "weight": 0.25
      }
    ]
  },
  "expected_benefit": "Restore intra-candidate parameter variation (non-zero objective std), enabling selection pressure and exploration; provides a clear signal to move away from collapsed population while still allowing optimization of performance.",
  "validation_plan": "The next iteration should include the 'parameter_spread' objective with weight 0.25. Success indicators: non-zero std for at least one objective (ideally parameter_spread > 0 and distance_from_center regains variance) and the optimizer can produce a spread of objective values across candidates. If objective std remains zero, escalate to investigate scorer application or candidate encoding.",
  "confidence": 0.70
}</decision>

Optimizer-generated identical candidates are the simplest explanation given the facts. Evidence: all three objectives have std = 0.0000 (performance mean=0.0155, parameter_spread mean=0.2113, distance_from_center mean=0.2129) and mutation_prob is currently 0.0 (no per-gene mutation) while random_candidate_ratio is 0.0. Change exactly one workflow parameter to re-enable stochastic variation.

